course: dictionary
lesson: 11612
title: Apprehend: catch or understand
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Apprehend is a formal word with two meanings. The first is to catch and arrest someone. «The police apprehended the thief outside the bank.» The police caught him and took him away, so apprehended means caught and arrested.
explain: The second meaning is to understand something. «It took her a while to apprehend the problem.» This is a formal way of saying she finally understood it. Read the words around the word to decide which meaning fits.
explain: Use the context check: swap in a simple word, like caught or understood, and see if the sentence still makes sense. If it does, you have the right meaning.
fact: Apprehend means to catch and arrest someone, or to understand something.
fact: «Apprehend» is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in news reports, detective stories and formal writing.
fact: Useful phrases: apprehend a suspect, apprehended by police.
fact: «Apprehended» is the past tense: yesterday the police apprehended the suspect.
fact: Do not confuse «apprehend» with «apprehensive», which means worried about something that might happen.
exercise: «The police apprehended the suspect at the station.» What does apprehended mean here? | Lost sight of | Thanked warmly | Hid from | *Caught and arrested
exercise: «It took him a while to apprehend the joke.» What does apprehend mean here? | *Understand | Repeat loudly | Tell | Forget
exercise: Find and copy the word that means caught and arrested: «The officers apprehended the driver after the chase.» | driver | chase | *apprehended | officers
test: «Two officers apprehended the man who stole the bike.» What does apprehended mean? | Waved at | Gave a present to | *Caught and arrested | Let go
test: «Once she had read the instructions, she could apprehend how the machine worked.» What does apprehend mean? | Break | *Understand | Lose | Ignore
exam: «The detectives hope to apprehend the thief before dark.» What does apprehend mean here? | Thank | Forgive | *Catch and arrest | Photograph
